Round 30 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
- Change: `aot_can_force_strict_tag(...)` now includes `DP0/DP1`.
- Effect path:
  - `aot_try_mat_dp_ctr_match(...)` previously treated nested-DP payloads (`cell_tag=DP0/DP1`) as immediate `non_ctr` misses.
  - Now it may run one local `aot_force_whnf_local(...)` on that payload and retry constructor/ext checks.
  - This keeps the existing tri-state probe contract intact (`0/1/2`) and reuses existing miss/mismatch semantics.

Why this mattered
- Previous telemetry showed dominant MAT-DP misses were `non_ctr_pre[tag=3/4]` (nested DP payloads), especially on `gab_takl` and `mat_mul`.
- Allowing DP payload local forcing converts many of those misses into `hits`/`ext_miss`, reducing generic strict-path DUP traffic.

Validation
- Build: `cd clang && clang -O2 -o main main.c`
- Tests: `./test/_all_.sh` passed.
- Admission sweep (`HVM_AOT_DEOPT=1 --as-c -s -T1`) stayed deopt-clean:
  - `AOT_DEOPT total=0` on all 17 admission benchmarks.
  - Residual captures unchanged and tiny: `gab_takl` (`APP_ARG_CAPTURE=3`), `mat_mul` (`CTR_FIELD_CAPTURE=3`), others `0`.

