Key lessons
- A large class of strict-MAT DP misses was unlockable by reusing existing local-WHNF force machinery on nested DP payloads.
- This is much higher leverage than ext-miss-only shortcut.
- DP local forcing does not, by itself, solve all DUP pressure (e.g. `trie_bitwise` remains dominated elsewhere).

Guardrails preserved
- No arg consumption on probe status `2` (ext mismatch fast path) — keep existing semantics.
- Step-limited semantics unchanged (all probe fast paths still preserve fallback behavior).

Next likely steps
1) Investigate remaining heavy DUP sources outside MAT-DP (`trie_bitwise` dominant `WNF_DUP_NOD`).
2) Revisit tiny residual captures in `gab_takl`/`mat_mul` (`APP_ARG_CAPTURE` / `CTR_FIELD_CAPTURE`) only if they show measurable runtime cost.
3) If needed, add a stricter bounded DP-on-DP composition path to avoid full local-WHNF force cost on some nested chains.
